From: K2B_RetroArch
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: kickpi-k2b: GPU OPPs (600 MHz), CPU cooling map, 1512 MHz

Port of the Orange Pi Zero3's 0050 and 0051 to the K2B: the same SoC, the
same AXP313A rails (dcdc1 GPU 810-990 mV, dcdc2 CPU 810-1100 mV) and the same
CPU speed grade (its table stops at 1416 MHz). GPU: 432 MHz @ 900 mV and
600 MHz @ 960 mV with devfreq. CPU: cooling map on the passive trip, trips
80/90 C, 1512 MHz at the 1.10 V that 1416 MHz already uses.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-kickpi-k2b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-kickpi-k2b.dts
@@ -413,3 +413,70 @@
 	status = "okay";
 	usb1_vbus-supply = <&reg_usb_vbus>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * GPU operating points (port of the Zero3's 0050). Mainline and Armbian have
+ * none for the H616/H618, so the Mali-G31 ran fixed at 432 MHz with no
+ * devfreq. Values from Orange Pi's BSP (sun50i-h616.dtsi gpu_opp_table):
+ * 432 MHz (kept at 900 mV) and 600 MHz @ 960 mV. Its 800 MHz @ 1080 mV is left
+ * out: above this board's dcdc1 maximum (990 mV, as on the Zero3).
+ * panfrost's simple_ondemand devfreq moves to 600 MHz only under load.
+ */
+&gpu {
+	operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
+};
+
+/ {
+	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+		opp-432000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <432000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <900000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * CPU thermal protection and 1512 MHz (port of the Zero3's 0051).
+ *
+ * The H616 dtsi defines cpu-thermal trips (60/70 C passive) but binds no
+ * cooling device, so only the 110 C critical trip ever acted. Bind the CPUs to
+ * the first passive trip and raise both to 80/90 C, so normal play is not
+ * throttled, while a run that gets hot is.
+ *
+ * 1512 MHz: sun50i-h616-cpu-opp.dtsi offers it only to speed grades 1, 3, 5.
+ * This K2B's chip, like the Zero3's, stops at 1416 MHz (grade 0 or 2), which
+ * runs at 1.10 V, the vdd-cpu (dcdc2) maximum in this dts. Allow 1512 MHz at
+ * that SAME 1.10 V. An overclock for these grades; no voltage is raised.
+ */
+&cpu_threshold {
+	temperature = <80000>;
+};
+
+&cpu_target {
+	temperature = <90000>;
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/cpu-thermal} {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map0 {
+			trip = <&cpu_threshold>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>,
+					 <&cpu1 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>,
+					 <&cpu2 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>,
+					 <&cpu3 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&{/opp-table-cpu/opp-1512000000} {
+	opp-microvolt-speed0 = <1100000>;
+	opp-microvolt-speed2 = <1100000>;
+	opp-supported-hw = <0x2f>;
+};
